      "name": "ig-build-pipeline",
      "title": "ig-build-pipeline",
      "description": "The bare FHIR IG pipeline — FSH to SUSHI to the IG Publisher to a pages branch, with no pre-processing and no post-processing. What this layer runs, what it emits, and the list of things it deliberately refuses to know about. Owns the AST cache lifecycle: an IG site is built from the AST on its cache branch, the publish refuses a stale one, and the reusable `ig-ast-refresh.yml` is the one writer. Owns what an IG reader may read: `contentTypes.ig.include` in the repository's `index.config.json`, and the legacy warning for a repository that declares none. Read before adding anything to fhir-harness, before onboarding, converting or changing the workflows of an IG repository, and before publishing an IG site.",
